{"bug":"K001","report":"B","v":"missed","ref":"5. Rewriting Implode entries discards required compression flags","evidence":"“flags() discards the original compression-specific bits.” This concerns Implode metadata rewriting; the report does not identify Shrink's exclusion of code 8191/MAX_CODE or resulting full-table decoding failures."}
{"bug":"K002","report":"D","v":"partial","ref":"Stream visitors silently receive no additional metadata","evidence":"“the visitor silently suppresses the resulting error” and “zero metadata callbacks while returning success.” The report identifies header consumption and suppressed parsing failure, but does not identify the consequent failure to apply central-directory Unix permissions during stream extraction."}
{"bug":"K004","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"6. finish_into_readable() exposes ZIP64 sentinels as actual sizes","evidence":"“fails with `Invalid checksum` when read to completion.” This concerns incorrect ZIP64 sizes, not an empty destination buffer causing premature CRC validation before entry EOF. The required empty-read defect is absent throughout the report."}
{"bug":"K005","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"1. Append and merge lose required ZIP64 offsets","evidence":"“Parsing removes ZIP64 extra fields, but central-directory writing does not regenerate them.” This concerns existing entries becoming unreadable after rewriting, not acceptance of a zero-entry EOCD with an unchecked offset followed by append-driven output inflation."}
